# The scoreboard logs are append-only, and two writers touch them: the CI run
# and any local run. Git's default merge treats concurrent appends as a
# conflict, which in CI means the "Commit scoreboard" step's rebase retry can
# never succeed on its own — a day's graded outcomes would sit unpushed until
# someone resolved it by hand.
#
# union takes both sides' lines instead. Order is not meaningful in these files
# (every row carries its own timestamp) and scoreboard.py de-duplicates by date
# on load, so a row appearing twice cannot double-count in the accuracy stats.
*.jsonl merge=union
